{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-golden-ratio-degeneration-brings","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:golden-ratio-degeneration-brings","kind":"remark","title":"Golden-ratio cusp and the sub-classical regime $q<1$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-descartes-elliptic-curve"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-descartes-elliptic-curve","tags":["elliptic-curve","descartes","golden-ratio","cusp","substrate-parameter"],"text":"golden-ratio-degeneration-brings.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:golden-ratio-degeneration-brings\"></a><p><strong>Golden ratio degeneration.</strong>\nThe second Weierstrass coefficient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r(q)</code> contains the factor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(s^2 + s - 1)</code> in its numerator. This vanishes at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s = (\\sqrt{5} - 1)/2 = 1/\\varphi</code>, the reciprocal of the golden ratio <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi = (1 + \\sqrt{5})/2</code>. At this value <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1/\\varphi^2 = (3 - \\sqrt{5})/2 \\approx 0.382</code>, the curve <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{E}_q</code> acquires a cusp. The elliptic fiber degenerates and the color fibration becomes singular.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/golden-ratio-degeneration-brings.md","heading":"Remark","number":"8.8.20","page":"b/rem-golden-ratio-degeneration-brings","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
